Article 8
(1) The forms of services for victims of violence organized by PPT include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for the purposes of evidence in the legal field;
c. legal aid services to assist victims of violence in undergoing the judicial process;
d. first psychosocial assistance to victims conducted to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims;
e. accompaniment of victims of violence carried out by competent persons or institutions that have the expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of victims of violence and have cooperated with PPT; and
f. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and provision of economic access so that victims can be independent.
(2) The service mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) regulated by Regent Regulation.

